    "kind": "exercise-or-check",
    "locator": "chunk 2",
    "text": "Topic 28 -- Taylor and Maclaurin Series \nWe\u2019ve seen a few situations where we can create a power series \nrepresentation of a function by careful \u201Crestructuring\u201D of a known function \nand/or with the use of differentiation and integration. \nIs there a more general approach? \nSuppose that a function has a power series representation: \n\uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC65) = \u2211 \uD835\uDC50\uD835\uDC5B(\uD835\uDC65 \u2212 \uD835\uDC4E)\uD835\uDC5B\n\u221E\n\uD835\uDC5B=0\n= \uD835\uDC500 \u002B \uD835\uDC501(\uD835\uDC65 \u2212 \uD835\uDC4E) \u002B \uD835\uDC502(\uD835\uDC65 \u2212 \uD835\uDC4E)2 \u002B \uD835\uDC503(\uD835\uDC65 \u2212 \uD835\uDC4E)3 \u002B \u22EF",
    "tokenCount": 62,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0003",
    "ordinal": 3,
    "kind": "heading",
    "locator": "chunk 3",
    "text": "# PAGE 2\nPage 2 of 15",
    "tokenCount": 6,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0004",
    "ordinal": 4,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 4",
    "text": "Conclusions: \nIf \uD835\uDC53 has a power series representation (expansion) at \uD835\uDC4E, that is, if  \n\uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC65) = \u2211 \uD835\uDC50\uD835\uDC5B(\uD835\uDC65 \u2212 \uD835\uDC4E)\uD835\uDC5B\n\u221E\n\uD835\uDC5B=0\n          |\uD835\uDC65 \u2212 \uD835\uDC4E| \u003C \uD835\uDC45 \nThen, its coefficients are given by the formula \n\uD835\uDC50\uD835\uDC5B = \uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC5B)(\uD835\uDC4E)\n\uD835\uDC5B!  \nSo, the expansion at \uD835\uDC65 = \uD835\uDC4E is given by: \n\uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC65) = \uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC4E) \u002B \uD835\uDC53\u2032(\uD835\uDC4E)\n1! (\uD835\uDC65 \u2212 \uD835\uDC4E) \u002B \uD835\uDC53\u2032\u2032(\uD835\uDC4E)\n2! (\uD835\uDC65 \u2212 \uD835\uDC4E)2 \u002B \uD835\uDC53\u2032\u2032\u2032(\uD835\uDC4E)\n3! (\uD835\uDC65 \u2212 \uD835\uDC4E)3 \u002B \u22EF",
    "tokenCount": 33,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0005",
    "ordinal": 5,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 5",
    "text": "\uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC65) = \u2211 \uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC5B)(\uD835\uDC4E)\n\uD835\uDC5B! (\uD835\uDC65 \u2212 \uD835\uDC4E)\uD835\uDC5B\n\u221E\n\uD835\uDC5B=0",
    "tokenCount": 1,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0006",
    "ordinal": 6,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 6",
    "text": "This is called the Taylor series of the function \uD835\uDC53 at \uD835\uDC4E.",
    "tokenCount": 10,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0007",
    "ordinal": 7,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 7",
    "text": "If we take the Taylor series and let \uD835\uDC4E = 0, \n\uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC65) = \u2211 \uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC5B)(0)\n\uD835\uDC5B! \uD835\uDC65\uD835\uDC5B\n\u221E\n\uD835\uDC5B=0",
    "tokenCount": 11,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0008",
    "ordinal": 8,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 8",
    "text": "\uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC65) = \uD835\uDC53(0) \u002B \uD835\uDC53\u2032(0)\n1! \uD835\uDC65 \u002B \uD835\uDC53\u2032\u2032(0)\n2! \uD835\uDC652 \u002B \uD835\uDC53\u2032\u2032\u2032(0)\n3! \uD835\uDC653 \u002B \u22EF \nThis is called the Maclaurin series of \uD835\uDC53.",
    "tokenCount": 16,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0009",
    "ordinal": 9,
    "kind": "heading",
    "locator": "chunk 9",
    "text": "# PAGE 3\nPage 3 of 15",
    "tokenCount": 6,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0010",
    "ordinal": 10,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 10",
    "text": "Examples \nDetermine a series representation for \uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC65) = \uD835\uDC52 \uD835\uDC65 about \uD835\uDC65 = 0.  Find the \nassociated radius of convergence.",
    "tokenCount": 14,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0011",
    "ordinal": 11,
    "kind": "heading",
    "locator": "chunk 11",
    "text": "# PAGE 4\nPage 4 of 15",
    "tokenCount": 6,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0012",
    "ordinal": 12,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 12",
    "text": "Determine a series representation for \uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC65) = cos \uD835\uDC65 about \uD835\uDC65 = 0.  Find the \nassociated radius of convergence.",
    "tokenCount": 14,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0013",
    "ordinal": 13,
    "kind": "heading",
    "locator": "chunk 13",
    "text": "# PAGE 5\nPage 5 of 15",
    "tokenCount": 6,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0014",
    "ordinal": 14,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 14",
    "text": "Determine a series representation for \uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC65) = sin \uD835\uDC65 about \uD835\uDC65 = 0.  Find the \nassociated radius of convergence.",
    "tokenCount": 14,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0015",
    "ordinal": 15,
    "kind": "heading",
    "locator": "chunk 15",
    "text": "# PAGE 6\nPage 6 of 15",
    "tokenCount": 6,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0016",
    "ordinal": 16,
    "kind": "paragraph",
    "locator": "chunk 16",
    "text": "Determine a series representation for \uD835\uDC53(\uD835\uDC65) = ln\u2061(1 \u002B \uD835\uDC65) about \uD835\uDC65 = 0.  Find the \nassociated radius of convergence.",
    "tokenCount": 15,
    "ocrConfidence": null
  },
  {
    "id": "src-20260726002931-b9da9d806a:chunk-0017",
    "ordinal": 17,
    "kind": "heading",
    "locator": "chunk 17",
    "text": "# PAGE 7\nPage 7 of 15",
